 ## Background
-Hash Grid Loss was introduced in the context of ECoNGS (Efficient Compressive Neural Gaussian Splats for Volume Visualization) [S1]. It is part of a two-stage optimization process where the hash grid component is optimized for compression alongside anchor attributes. The method leverages the concept of entropy coding, where the bit cost of a symbol is proportional to the negative logarithm of its probability [S1]. By minimizing this loss, the model learns to distribute the hash grid values in a way that minimizes the expected bit length of the encoded structure.
